 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "oven wont come on"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "If your oven has not come on recently or there was a brief power cut, the clock/programmer often defaults to 'Automatic' mode and will not allow heating until you set the time and switch it to 'Manual'. Please check if the clock is flashing; if so, set the current time and select Manual mode (often a hand symbol). If the clock is already set correctly or this doesn't work, please try setting the oven to 180°C on the Fan function for 15 minutes and let me know if it gets warm."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "yes its flashing 0.00 and a little symbol. i dont have the manual tho, how do i set the time?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That flashing display suggests the clock has reset (likely after a brief power cut), which puts the oven into an automatic mode where it won't heat until you set the time and switch it to Manual. To do this without the manual: press the 'Time' or clock button; use the '+'/'-' buttons or the temperature knob to adjust the hours, then press 'Time/Set' again for minutes. Once the correct time is shown, look for a 'Manual' button (often a hand symbol) and press it. This should allow you to select a function like Fan Oven at 180°C."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok i'll try that. i set the time and it came on and heated"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That is excellent news. To avoid this happening again in future, try not to isolate the oven at the wall switch unless necessary; if you do need to cut power, remember to reset the clock and select Manual mode when you turn it back on. Is there anything else I can help you with today?"
  }
 ],
